The LCUSP combustion chamber makes use of two additively-manufactured GRCop-84 axially-split halves,
joined with a circumferential electron beam weld in the barrel section. This full copper chamber is then cladded with
an Inconel 625 jacket and manifolds using Electron Beam Freeform Fabrication (EBF^3). The diameter of this
chamber maximized the 250x250 mm build area of the available powder bed machines. Larger-scale powder bed
machines such as the EOS M400
